---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { business, fullAddress } from '../data/site';

const effective = 'October 3, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Fort Walton Beach Bowl"
  description="What the Fort Walton Beach Bowl website collects, why, and how it's used. No cookies, no tracking, no selling your information."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" lede="Short version: we only collect what you send us in the party form, we use it to reply, and that's it." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="fine-print">Effective {effective}</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website belongs to {business.name}, {fullAddress}. You can reach us at
        <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The quick summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, no ads, no cookies and no tracking.</li>
        <li>We only collect what you type into the party inquiry form.</li>
        <li>We use it to reply about your party. We don't sell it, rent it or use it for marketing.</li>
        <li>We never take payments or card details on this website.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>The party inquiry form</h3>
      <p>When you send a party inquiry, we receive:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your phone number and/or email address</li>
        <li>Your preferred date and number of guests</li>
        <li>What you're planning and any notes you add</li>
        <li>Your confirmation that you're 18 or older</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We use this only to answer your inquiry and plan your event. We'll contact you by the phone number or email you gave
        us about that party, and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h3>Technical information</h3>
      <p>
        Like any website, our hosting provider automatically records basic technical details when you visit, such as your IP
        address, browser type and the pages you request. This is used to deliver the site and keep it secure, not to track
        you.
      </p>

      <h2>Who handles it</h2>
      <p>
        Our website and form are hosted by Netlify, which delivers form submissions to us and may run them through automated
        spam filtering. Netlify handles that information under its own privacy policy. We don't share your information with
        anyone else unless the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep party inquiries only as long as we need them to plan your event, then delete them.</p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This website isn't directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect personal information from them.
        The party form is for parents, guardians and adults 18 or older, and it asks you not to include children's full
        names, birthdates or photos. If you think a child has sent us personal information, call us and we'll delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website doesn't use cookies, analytics, advertising trackers or social media pixels. Our fonts and images load
        from our own site, not from third parties. If we ever add analytics, we'll choose a privacy-friendly tool and
        update this policy first.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments and reservations</h2>
      <p>
        We don't take payments on this website. Online party reservations are made on Bowling Passport's website, under
        their privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to Facebook, Google Maps and Bowling Passport. When you follow those links, their privacy policies apply,
        not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what information you've sent us, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Just call
        <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change how we handle information, we'll update this page and the effective date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .prose h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
</style>
